              <p class=3D"corner-intro">A collection of web design and deve=
lopment news and thoughts from CodePen's own Chris Coyier.</p>=0D=0A       =
                   </mj-raw>=0D=0A                          <h3>Check It B4=
 U Wreck It</h3>=0A<p>There is an airport in Bend, Oregon where I live. We=
=E2=80=99ve got a proper one in Redmond, the next town over, but a little b=
aby municipal one here in Bend. There is a cafe there that I=E2=80=99m only=
 just hearing about: <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/HpIbO_dyu=
aRHxW_k-1kCGg~~/AABEfhA~/plyrfXvEfuNzcJ4sTzlrQWXWPIKthYlhzZ1BD94Edwa7ximVQ1=
ot8bY2tm-PaFf_H8TQHajuGWxOOIKMNk8vtEwv4Pcvuu8veO_2fO7sGQxwcJpUmGuoNAu-p_94e=
3Ks">Bend Airport Cafe</a>. Looks nice, I should go!</p>=0A<p>I=E2=80=99m m=
entioning it for another reason, though. As soon as I saw that website, I S=
AW CLAUDE CODE immediately.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-em=
ail-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=
=3Dauto/codepen-spark/i_see_claude.jpg" alt=3D"On the left, the website for=
 the Bend Airport Cafe. On the right, the kid from The Sixth Sense saying '=
I see dead people', but 'dead people' is crossed out and replaced with 'Cla=
ude'." width=3D"500"/>=0A<p>Tell me I=E2=80=99m not crazy and you=E2=80=99v=
e seen it too.</p>=0A<p>This <em>look</em> is <em>everywhere</em>. To my ey=
es, it=E2=80=99s more prevalent than Bootstrap ever was, Tailwind UI, or ev=
en the purple-gradient-text era of crypto and early AI.</p>=0A<p>I feel lik=
e it happened as Anthropic started talking about skills and <a href=3D"http=
s://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/_ebUt3OExdPuLcHIxZCWjg~~/AABEfhA~/twnCDY_MLEi=
MWanIraIko8tD8HR2zhQKcFIm5wMb4lXKpGQuDSCu7W7-r8Fjc1809U33FDHjO054XRwnR5-gx9=
yiMYmPaftSZq7mLihX6QN7tZhlT4JFqs9rotIdF1aioYLMvN0AflfxtgXPHa3jIbuxfXdznCUje=
trjzK4gg9s~">made their own design skill</a>. The designs coming out of Cla=
ude Code are undeniably much nicer, but do look very same-y, like they have=
 some pretty strict prompts baked in that choose between a very limited sub=
set of design choices.</p>=0A<p>About this particular restaurant website, I=
 feel like it=E2=80=99s quite decent looking and I don=E2=80=99t hate that =
maybe the design bar for low-end work gets pushed higher because of this, b=
ut also HEY EVERYBODY, let=E2=80=99s keep a close watch on all this. <stron=
g>These AI slop websites are chockablock with really simple mistakes</stron=
g>.</p>=0A<p>The navigation of the site is mostly jump links like <code>#ca=
tering</code>, which work fine when on the homepage. But the =E2=80=9CGalle=
ry=E2=80=9D page links to <code>/gallery</code>, and when you=E2=80=99re on=
 that page, the jump links don=E2=80=99t work anymore. Even the logo is jus=
t a link to <code>#</code>, so when you=E2=80=99re not on the homepage, it =
doesn=E2=80=99t get you back there.</p>=0A<figure><img src=3D"https://produ=
ction-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,qual=
ity=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/bend_airport_cafe_source.png" alt=3D"D=
eveloper tools open on the unclickable logo from the airport cafe website. =
" width=3D"450"/> <figcaption>Now I can=E2=80=99t get back to the homepage =
from any sub page unless I hand-alter the URL.</figcaption></figure>=0A<p>I=
 was reading Piccalilli=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/=
f/a/WmrN4rIvIEycAXdO_-GUaQ~~/AABEfhA~/AC2ybUNds7X9IXN-y7OI2_iaf4E1DtzWcSNAU=
WAa74kK2FOVDTiGtZCvx7TQ4t_RG2L1VURTrrx9ROvrwEOZUA7A5wJE5AewGwCdybaQhtRcDg0h=
t8WHj9QIaf9gqt-Tj8HHCRldrQZege-KoTw8mcrsYi5ojcV7nSLXHeHnF60L2rynMqQCj1Vnt9V=
mtzFW">in-depth guide to customising lists with CSS</a> and thinking about =
what a nice touch customized lists are. Oh look, a nice customized list! Na=
h, just kidding, it=E2=80=99s a totally unsemantic div soup with a bunch of=
 Tailwind classes.</p>=0A<figure><img src=3D"https://production-codepen-ema=
il-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=
=3Dauto/codepen-spark/bend_airport_source2.png" alt=3D"Developer tools open=
 on the class soup on the 'customized list items' in the menu. " width=3D"4=
50"/><figcaption>This is so chill to do now on real lists with <code>::mark=
er</code>.</figcaption></figure>=0A<hr />=0A<p>This is what extra got me go=
ing the other day. Then I heard about <em>another</em> restaurant in Bend f=
or the first time: <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/QEh2PP1WDos=
Gvkr2AexlSw~~/AABEfhA~/CAPl_ggn3t_dhTe5nuHO64_hHAKRDLVSqzqHI5t9hxxv2iu3eQfz=
c_Jzh19m3rAp0SJ0p_nw_9oIImaIOvmMeLLvrVrX4guYsP5W8SmXd7qqxc7bs4Ez6CokAL1Bzae=
w">Los Andes</a>.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets=
.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/co=
depen-spark/los_andes_website.png" alt=3D"The homepage of Los Andes. The fo=
od looks good. The site, well, it does not. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>I know y=
ou can just <em>smell</em> the Claude design skill wafting off that sucker.=
</p>=0A<p>It doesn=E2=80=99t just look the same though, it=E2=80=99s full o=
f <em>simple</em> mistakes. Like the one-field form doesn=E2=80=99t associa=
te the label correctly.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-=
assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dau=
to/codepen-spark/los_andes_source.png" alt=3D"Developer tools open on the l=
abel, disconnected from the form. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>The light gray tex=
t used isn=E2=80=99t even close to readable, even for someone with strong v=
ision.</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.codepenass=
ets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/=
los_andes_source2.png" alt=3D"Developer tools open on the lightest, lightes=
t possible gray and tiniest, tiniest font. Sheesh. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>T=
here is a little irony to me in that surely Clade Code could help anyone fi=
x these problems so <em>quickly and easily</em>. But either people don=E2=
=80=99t know they are even problems or don=E2=80=99t care and both of those=
 options are a bummer.</p>=0A<p>The same-y design choices are such a hilari=
ous tell though. I had it help with adding design to <a href=3D"https://go.=
sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/1FLK739zVD6kASZ7zN4cgw~~/AABEfhA~/vqmhQigLQm4dQ172eY=
u5WaUT8WqrK09YRIFUFM07_vlGVkOU8NPOqJ3y0XWGPE5gB1plRImMii8w-yz1sBsvC585LYIYx=
91BKZ9JRKf8wxeIJEMLlnAEwwWldIaNBugNPZ3eKfmAXqnkXWnfxHM31nvOdu_aUT5HLjVAljSs=
AqWUEahkxBLebPXkyZaVdCht9qBtsSmzRkefqi92HjXBp-RgTQ107Wpk_5M3P0oIaOs~">a Vue=
 Template</a> a while back, and honestly it looks pretty great I think! But=
 it=E2=80=99s 100% that same exact design aesthetic happening here too.</p>=
=0A<p>The one-word-is-italic-in-the-header is hilariously common to me, alo=
ng with the one-button-is-outline-one-is-solid, and the little-tiny all-cap=
s header above headlines. BASK IN IT:</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://production-=
codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D=
90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/the_usual_claude_stuff.png" alt=3D"Well, her=
e it is again: Claude's new 'elegant' style. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>The one=
 that gets me the most is how every =E2=80=9Ccard=E2=80=9D style element ha=
s a dang hover on it though. <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/l=
3auJd_gG-yRJi52sf5ziw~~/AABEfhA~/0-tM6LPkjvy4EO8IHDrLhIqyaOk8OfUcCBboTWJsPb=
DZWH99i2mWP1UjxV-xUaubKeOTdZXhPPjm2YYpN0l9moNJkPqMzW9U9JF-TWsgB2VkUsxIcA0Tw=
c5WtwP5_fqvicqrBFgrPz9gIVUh2-GdZBVOMy-QYCw1QYIciTzyIRJXcpU0O0YJPHLJK-vlNe13=
">It=E2=80=99s just everywhere</a>. And it can be a real problem. It means =
that sometimes it=E2=80=99s an <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;button&g=
t;</code> wrapping the entire contents of a card, meaning a title, copy, im=
age, etc, which is just silly. Seriously, they <a href=3D"https://go.sparkp=
ostmail2.com/f/a/lrsS_YPrqG5_3dHTgX-Eeg~~/AABEfhA~/WEQ--ftQp8pJqxEATUux5byx=
CG30Kp2vb9kc8AxGKElQ-fsfzVuevPPqlxIjvJaq2D7Zy4srwMugKLqCdGm1rMjR01GEPT1I0ZL=
VNR8dwnGAhvM_M89mku60TZPHKYhQVsAOdB-gTTLvRYc1cflLPbm5_OAeG89ZIZ-E44v2mhVHtM=
AjAlzkZvjIOYfd1qNb">need to read this</a>.</p>=0A<hr />=0A<p>Lemme leave yo=
u with some good articles.</p>=0A<ul>=0A<li>Dave writes about approaching l=
ight/dark styles at a component level, with optional inversion, <a href=3D"=
https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/7BxQORTDZ4ruFx_XEE5gMg~~/AABEfhA~/LewrRGu=
2PuzDX3CPMBbBp4ZvigNs9cfJsT7sJ1HZWd4OH4KQWRWqhMFvd4ypBkgVoxQ00CfEaBDWIJ3_Yg=
tOAuLuwFvueCxgma6vB_H01u1hd2XWWbp2g9lsL9Ux6ytYwVzPEC0p6iK0zTPcrW3g5MrwGKGOr=
GToNgACkYOJgCw~">made quite simple really</a>.</li>=0A<li><a href=3D"https:=
//go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/d84sp8v5ouRuUQi53eIfnA~~/AABEfhA~/AC2ybUNds7X9I=
XN-y7OI24_iVx26pYJTiatkJ8ABf-CfO4n9zeHZxqUY4UdlrGbxaZonaIBB_GemR4jYvlj3z2Gr=
PdzyJkMYgqINtrgpouK-zNPv3M_hS4XReb2NieqZWQkZTCRGs6va8nbe-_HJ9iKgUHcxcHq5ltZ=
TNu27-wKLsnNvvnduA_XDvWikmhR0">Eric writes about the <code>infinity</code> =
keyword in CSS</a>. I love the use case where using it with <code>word-spac=
ing</code> forces one-word-per-line. Clever.</li>=0A<li>Roma writes about <=
a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/tJxlPHeRYX_YPvq4ILi4ag~~/AABEfh=
A~/l3_2x3DvHJurlgDExhB-xQJzXhrlBEmI08QVz_sxB3mipIFE27SURyikQYtrxbrbKpNp7mPe=
5nGdF-XH8yGg71g6MfhUXc6Hld-F-M67rIVYu3YLUjxTszaEBObVak9sqcz-MsAqxZ2ecohb68r=
wtg~~">Responsive Cyclic Margins</a> with some absolutely wacky clamp/max f=
unctions in order to get truncation of text happening at the end of text an=
d <em>before</em> an icon. Just try to get that right, Claude.</li>=0A</ul>=
